          <change when="2013-03-20T07:44:28.859-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/berkes.lajos">Vote - AcceptText - Both suggestions are convincing. I've checked them againt the image on the cd-rom of Harrauer's paleography. &#xD;
In l2, I'm inclined to write &lt;:(εὐκ̣λ̣(εεστάτῳ))|alt|(εὐκ̣(λεεστάτῳ)):&gt;, since Morelli says: 'dopo il nome dell'emiro e prima del titolo si deve leggere εὐκ̣λ̣(εεστάτῳ) o εὐκ̣(λεεστάτῳ).'</change>
          <change when="2013-03-17T10:47:04.746-04:00" who="https://papyri.info/editor/users/ngonis">I changed two readings: in line 2, the suggestion (the first of the two) recorded in CPR XXX, p. 201, 9 n., is certain (I had arrived at the same reading independently), and I incorporated it into the text; in 14, the new reading is suggested by the plate.</change>
